Even though the probability distributions overlap in time, two photons originating from one laser pulse are always emitted into orthogonal time modes (see Supplementary Information) and only averaging over many repetitions induces the statistical overlap.

Turning to the spectral analysis, we employ a tunable filter that enables us to frequency-resolve either the overall emission or, in a heralded manner, the two-photon signal (see inset Fig.~\ref{fig2}b and Methods).
% To this end, we add a pair of etalons (see Methods) to one of the HBT paths (compare inset of Fig.~\ref{fig2}b).
