The PFC's exceptional vulnerability stems from four critical factors:

\begin{enumerate}
\item \textbf{Extreme Metabolic Demand}: Highest ATP consumption per gram of any brain tissue (up to 20\,\% of total brain glucose consumption despite being only 4\,\% of brain mass) \cite{7};
\item \textbf{Steepest Inverted-U Curve}: Requires precisely titrated $\deff$ levels within a narrow 80--120\,\% range;
\item \textbf{D1-Dominant Architecture}: A high $D_1:D_2$ ratio of approximately 4:1 biases the region toward excitation and vulnerability to excitotoxicity \cite{8};
\item \textbf{Massive Connectivity}: Most dependent on coordinated network activity across distant brain regions.
\end{enumerate}
