\subsection{The Seizure Paradox: Global Excess, Prefrontal Collapse}

This regional heterogeneity leads to one of the theory's most counterintuitive predictions:

\begin{hypothesis}[The Prefrontal Collapse Hypothesis]
During generalized seizures, while subcortical dopamine release reaches extreme levels, the prefrontal cortex experiences paradoxical depletion of effective dopamine signaling due to metabolic exhaustion and excitotoxic stunning \cite{9}.
\end{hypothesis}

Figure \ref{fig:seizure_paradox_detailed} illustrates this paradox, which explains several clinical observations including post-ictal confusion, amnesia surrounding seizure events, and why consciousness is lost despite massive subcortical activation.
