\subsection{Dataset}

We analysed the Parkinson’s Progression Markers Initiative (PPMI)
v2025-06 release (download 25 June 2025).  
The subset used here contains
\textbf{70\,290} nights from \textbf{242} participants with at least one
valid sleep-metrics CSV and actigraphy stage file.  
File-level inclusion/exclusion logic exactly follows the
Python script \texttt{ppmi\_rem\_pipeline.py} (see Code Availability).

\subsection{Data-processing pipeline}

Figure~\ref{fig:pipeline_schematic} provides a schematic of the data-processing workflow;
key steps-implemented in \texttt{ppmi\_rem\_pipeline.py}-are:

\begin{enumerate}[label=\arabic*.]
\item \textbf{I/O \& sanity checks.}  
      All raw CSVs are read with \texttt{pandas~=~2.2.2}.  
      A helper \texttt{load\_csv()} aborts rows with \texttt{on\_bad\_lines="skip"}.
\item \textbf{Nightly REM metrics.}  
      Each epoch file is collapsed to \emph{REM minutes}, \emph{REM bouts}
      ($>60$ s inter-bout gap), and \emph{REM latency} (minutes).
\item \textbf{Clinical merge.}  
      Levodopa-Equivalent Daily Dose \textbf{(LEDD)}, demographics, clinical status and questionnaire tables
      are brought to \texttt{patno–infodt} tidy format
      [\texttt{patno} = patient number; \texttt{infodt} = visit date];  
      merges use an \emph{as-of join} so that each night inherits the most-recent clinical record.
\item \textbf{Medication flags.}  
      For every night we compute total \textbf{LEDD} and a binary
      \textbf{SSRI\_flag} (selective-serotonin-re-uptake-inhibitor exposure) using a
      compiled regular expression over drug names.
\item \textbf{Proteomics.}  
      Olink CSF and plasma datasets (normalised-protein-expression, \textbf{NPX}) are
      filtered to serotonergic markers-\textbf{HTR2A} (5-HT$_{2A}$ receptor),
      \textbf{TPH} (tryptophan hydroxylase) and \textbf{MAO} (mono-amine oxidase)-and pivoted wide.
\item \textbf{Export.}  
      The final table (\texttt{ppmi\_rem\_ready.parquet}; 70 290 rows, 48 columns) is written for downstream analysis.
\end{enumerate}

