\section{The Death Threshold: Understanding the Upper Limit}

\subsection{Why Consciousness Must Have Boundaries}

Evolution has shaped consciousness with hard limits because unlimited dopaminergic activation would prove rapidly lethal. The death threshold represents a fundamental biophysical constraint that has shaped the entire architecture of conscious experience.

\begin{equation}
\Viability(\DA) = \exp\left(-\left(\frac{\DA - \DA_{\text{lethal}}}{\sigma_{\text{death}}}\right)^4\right) \cdot \Theta(\DA_{\text{lethal}} - \DA)
\label{eq:death_threshold}
\end{equation}

\textbf{Parameter Definitions:}
\begin{itemize}
\item $\DA_{\text{lethal}} \approx 320\,\%$ baseline dopamine level. This value is a theoretical parameter estimated to align with the pathophysiology of lethal stimulant overdose, where synaptic concentrations can rise to extreme, excitotoxic levels \cite{Numachi2007}.
\item $\sigma_{\text{death}} \approx 15\,\%$ controls the sharpness of the death transition
\item $\Theta(x)$ is the Heaviside step function (0 for $x < 0$, 1 for $x \geq 0$)
\item The fourth power creates the sharp transition observed clinically
\end{itemize}
\subsection{Physiological basis for critical thresholds}
The value $\DA_{\text{lethal}}\!\approx\!320\,\%$ is grounded in
microdialysis data showing that a 1 mg kg\textsuperscript{-1} intravenous
cocaine bolus raises striatal dopamine to $319\pm35\,\%$ of baseline
while blocking $\approx\!89\,\%$ of DAT sites in rhesus
monkeys \cite{Nader2006}.  Higher doses risk seizures and
cardiorespiratory failure in both non-human primates and
humans \cite{Numachi2007}.  Conversely, serotonin toxicity requires
$\gtrsim\!40$‐fold basal 5-HT and becomes lethal only near
$10^{3}\!\times$ baseline \cite{Chiew2025}, substantiating the much wider
5-HT safety margin used in Eq. \ref{eq:5HT_safety}.  These empirical
bounds fix $\DA_{\max}$, $\DA_{\text{lethal}}$ and the
$\sigma_{\text{death}}$ term, while receptor-occupancy studies
(${\sim}80\%$ D\textsubscript{2} blockade \cite{Vermeulen2012}) justify
the steep $\beta_i$ values in Eq. \ref{eq:consciousness_multistate}.

