\section{Why \emph{5-HT\textsubscript{2A}} is Safe: The Complexity Modulator}

\subsection{Orthogonal Architecture}

Serotonin \emph{5-HT\textsubscript{2A}} receptors modulate consciousness along a dimension orthogonal to dopamine, explaining why their activation creates unique phenomenology without the lethal risks of dopaminergic excess. As demonstrated in Figure \ref{fig:system_comparison}, the \emph{5-HT\textsubscript{2A}} system operates through fundamentally different mechanisms than dopamine.

\subsection{The Desensitization Safety Valve}

The critical safety feature of \emph{5-HT\textsubscript{2A}} receptors is their rapid desensitization:

\begin{equation}
R_{\text{active}}(t) = R_{\text{total}} \cdot \exp\left(-\frac{t}{\tau_{\text{desens}}}\right) \cdot \left(1 - \frac{t}{t_{\text{tolerance}}}\right)
\label{eq:5HT_safety}
\end{equation}

With $\tau_{\text{desens}} \approx 2-4$ hours and $t_{\text{tolerance}} \approx 48-72$ hours, creating automatic protection against prolonged activation.

\section{Evolutionary Perspective: The Optimized Population}

\subsection{Why Psychosis Persists}

Despite its individual costs, psychosis-prone phenotypes are maintained in human populations at a stable frequency of 2--5\,\% \cite{11}. This may be because underlying traits confer certain exploratory or creative advantages at a group level, a concept known as balancing selection \cite{12}. The multi-modal validation protocol shown in Figure \ref{fig:validation_protocol} provides the framework for testing these evolutionary hypotheses.

