\paragraph{Clinical implications.} The adolescent peak in both dopamine and 5-HT$_{2A}$ systems creates a ``perfect storm'' for consciousness expansion but also vulnerability. This window coincides with:
\begin{itemize}
    \item Peak incidence of first-episode psychosis (ages 15--25)
    \item Maximum creative output in artistic domains
    \item Heightened susceptibility to both positive and negative drug experiences
    \item Formation of lifelong aesthetic and spiritual preferences
\end{itemize}

Conversely, the coordinated decline in late life explains the phenomenology of aging: reduced dream vividness, decreased openness to experience, and the protective effect against schizophrenia onset after age 40.
