(1+\varepsilon_n)\alpha_n -\beta_n.$
%\end{equation*}
Then $(\alpha_n)_\nnn$ converges and 
$\sum_\nnn \beta_n<\pinf$.
\end{fact}
\begin{proof}
This is a special deterministic case of 
a classical probabilistic result by Robbins and Siegmund \cite{RoSi}. 
See also \cite[Lemma~11 on page~50]{Polyak}, 
