    The Lipschitz bound in Proposition~\ref{p:Q}\ref{r:Qii}
is sharp. Indeed, taking $A = N_{\{0\}}$ yields $Q_{\beta\gets \alpha} = \tfrac{\beta}{\alpha}\Id $ which is $\tfrac{\beta}{\alpha}$-Lipschitz continuous.%$A = N_{\{1\}}$ yields $Q_{\beta\gets \alpha} = \tfrac{\beta}{\alpha}\Id + 1 - \tfrac{\beta}{\alpha}\Id$ which is $\tfrac{\beta}{\alpha}$-Lipschitz.
