\subsection{Parametric demiclosedness principle}
As mentioned in the introduction, resolvents --- and thus in particular the DR iteration operator in \eqref{e:0222d} --- are not necessarily weakly continuous. Browder's celebrated \emph{demiclosedness princple} \cite{MR230179} provides an alternative to assuming weak continuity of the operator in infinite-dimensional spaces. In this section, we investigate a parametric version of the demiclosedness principle. We start by recalling the principle as it is presented in \cite{BC2017}.

