While showing our sensitivity results to locate the CMB radius in figure~\ref{fig:result_measuring_cmb} of section~\ref{sec:results_cmb}, we present the $1\sigma$ bound on the $R_\text{CMB}$ radius as a function of true values of NSI parameters $\varepsilon_{\alpha\beta}$. In this appendix, we demonstrate the method to obtain these bounds for a representative choice of $\varepsilon^\text{true}_{\alpha\beta} = \pm \, 0.1$ and 0.

