\\[8pt]

\end{definition}
Over \(C\), we have that 5 is not radically representable, but \(r_5\) is representable by the radicals and \(BR\)
\[ w^5 + b \cdot w + 1 = 0, \]
i.e.,
\\[6pt]
\(\ \text{BRr}_5:(X)^5 \rightarrow\ Sym^5(X), \)
\\[6pt]
\( \vec{a}(a_1, a_2, \ldots, a_5) \, \vert \, \rightarrow
\begin{cases}
