When we want to solve this general form  using the two definitions

\[
  \{y = x^q, 
 x^{p} = c - \alpha \cdot y\} \iff 
\] 

\begin{equation} \tag{3.2.124} \label{2.3.114}
 y^{p/q} = c - \alpha \cdot y, 
\{p, q\} \in \mathbb{R}_{+} - \{0\} \quad 
\end{equation}

From \eqref{2.3.114} and from \eqref{2.3.113} to apply
\begin{equation}  \tag{3.2.125} \label{2.3.115}
x = \sqrt[p]{c - \alpha \cdot y} = \sqrt[p]{c - \alpha \cdot \sqrt[p/q]{c - \alpha \cdot \sqrt[p/q]{c - \cdots}}} , p/q > 1 
