The last relation \eqref{2.3.115} is the final solution of the \eqref{2.3.113} In the general form we request.

\textbf{3.10.9 For solving a 4 term equation, with periodic radicals of the form \( x^p + \alpha \cdot x^q + \beta \cdot x^v - c = 0 \) }: We should use its gradual adjustment to a trinomial equation of the form \eqref{2.3.113}, so that it can be resolved by this procedure. To better fit the process of radicals we find the increasing series of exponents i.e. we assume \( v < q < p \) and then using the 2 definitions:

